Z||000000||86se/lambo||01-31-2001||12:10 AM||||a while back i had a radiator cooling fan problem where the fan would not come on..and the temp. sensor and relays were good. when bench testing the fan it worked fine. here's the deal. Some fieros came with a heavy-duty 2-stage(speed) fan, most of these were dukes,infact thats what the haines manual lists them under.But thats what my fiero was wired for and its a 2.8. there is an optional code (something like vo6) that designates this..it was an optional purchase. Anyway when the car was stretched for the kit they accidentally gave me the one stage fan..and thats were the problem was. If your fan Has a ballist resistor(white ceramic thing with wires attatched) then you have the heavy duty fan. Big difference in price $300(dealer) for heavy duty vs $30(napa)for the single speed. i simply wired the fan so when the temp sensor grounded it first turn on the high speed..instead of the low (just changed the wires at the fan connector). The speed is a big difference and for a kit where the radiator lies flat.. or a fiero with cooling problems this would be an easy fix,if you have the heavy duty fan. simple mod.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-31-2001||11:33 AM||||My 84 had a 2 speed fan. It broke so I replaced it with the single speed fan.||||reg||1
